---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Bug1 = `local scores = {12, 8, 21, 3, 17}

for i = 1, #scores do
    local total = 0
    total = total + scores[i]
end

print("Total: " .. total)`;

const Bug2 = `local names = {"Ada", "Bo", "Cy"}

for i = 1, #names - 1 do
    print(names[i])
end`;

const Bug3 = `local lives = 3

while lives > 0 do
    print("Life " .. lives)
end

print("Game over")`;

const Bug4 = `local x = 20
local passes = 0

repeat
    passes = passes + 1
    x = x - 1
until x > 10

print("Passes: " .. passes)`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Debug Challenge: Loops</h1>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>
            Four short programs with loops in them, each with exactly one thing
            wrong. <b class="text-sn-theme">One of them will not stop.</b>
          </p>

          <div class="alert alert-warning">
            <b>Read before you run.</b> A program with a loop that never ends
            gives you a window that ignores you. If you do run it and it hangs,
            close the terminal panel and reopen it.
          </div>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="bugs">
          <h2>The Four Programs</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 1</h3>

          <p>
            This should add five numbers and print <code>Total: 61</code>. It
            stops with an error about a <code>nil</code> value instead.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug1} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Bug 1" class="mb-3" />

          <p class="text-body-secondary">
            <b>There are two things wrong here and they have the same cause.</b>{" "}
            Find the cause and both go away.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 2</h3>

          <p>
            Three names in the table, and it prints two of them.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug2} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Bug 2" class="mb-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 3</h3>

          <p>
            This should count down from 3 and then say <code>Game over</code>.
            It prints <code>Life 3</code> forever.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug3} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Bug 3" class="mb-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 4</h3>

          <p>
            This should keep going until <code>x</code> drops to 10, taking
            about ten passes. It takes <b>one</b>.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug4} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Bug 4" class="mb-3" />

          <p class="text-body-secondary">
            The loop itself is fine. Read the word before the condition.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>For each program, give:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>One sentence on what was wrong</li>
            <li>The corrected line of code</li>
            <li>
              For bug 3 only: <b>the general rule</b> that would have caught it
              before you ran anything
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">Count the passes on paper.</b> For each
            loop, write down what the condition is at the start of every pass.
            Four rows is usually enough to see the problem.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>5 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Debugging
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
